\"He doesn't have full control over it yet.\"

Sam looked at her.

\"How do you know?\"

\"I helped build the machine he's using.\"

Everyone stared at her.

Paxman took a step back.

\"You worked for Victor?\"

Ava lowered her head.

\"I didn't have a choice.\"

\"He captured my family years ago.\"

\"If I refused to help him, he threatened to hurt them.\"

Joseph's expression softened.

\"I'm sorry.\"

Ava looked up.

\"I escaped three days ago.\"

\"I came here because you're the only people who can stop him.\"

Joseph walked over to the giant map.

He pointed to Victor's fortress.

\"The Light Crystal is here.\"

Ava shook her head.

\"Not anymore.\"

Everyone looked at her.

\"Victor moved it this morning.\"

She reached into her pocket and unfolded a small map.

\"I stole this before I escaped.\"

She spread it across the table.

A hidden island sat in the middle of the ocean.

Surrounding it were sharp cliffs.

Only one narrow passage led inside.

\"What is this place?\" Sam asked.

\"The Black Fortress,\" Ava answered.

\"It's Victor's headquarters.\"

Paxman studied the drawing.

Guard towers.

Searchlights.

A massive steel gate.

\"This place looks impossible to get into.\"

Ava smiled.

\"That's exactly what Victor wants everyone to think.\"

