It echoed through every hallway of the fortress.

Nash barked toward the darkness.

Sam stepped in front of everyone.

\"What are Hunters?\" he asked.

Ava swallowed.

\"They aren't people.\"

The room fell silent.

Joseph slowly opened a storage cabinet and pulled out several flashlights.

He handed one to Paxman and another to Sam.

\"We're leaving. Now.\"

The group hurried through a long hallway.

The emergency lights flickered overhead.

Suddenly...

CLANG!

Something slammed into a steel door.

Everyone jumped.

Another loud bang followed.

The heavy door bent inward.

Paxman tightened his grip on his flashlight.

\"They're strong.\"

Ava nodded.

\"Very.\"

\"They were built to track anyone who escapes Victor.\"

Another crash echoed through the hallway.

CRACK!

The steel door burst open.

Three large machines stepped into the corridor.

Each one stood nearly eight feet tall.

Their eyes glowed bright red.

Metal claws scraped across the floor.

\"They found us,\" Joseph whispered.

The first Hunter let out a loud mechanical roar.

It charged.

\"Run!\" Sam shouted.

The group sprinted down the hallway.

The Hunters chased after them.

Their heavy footsteps shook the floor.

Nash stayed close beside Paxman.

The hallway suddenly ended.

Only one door stood in front of them.

Joseph quickly entered a code.

The keypad flashed red.

ACCESS DENIED.

\"Oh, no,\" Joseph muttered.

The Hunters were getting closer.

Sam looked around.

\"Move!\"

He planted his feet against the wall.

With all his strength, he slammed his shoulder into the door.

BOOM!

It didn't move.

The Hunters were only a few feet away now.

Paxman took a deep breath.

A blast of freezing air shot across the hallway.

Ice spread over the floor.

The first Hunter slipped.

It crashed into the other two.

The machines tumbled into a tangled pile.

\"Again!\" Joseph yelled.

Sam charged the door one more time.

CRASH!

This time the hinges snapped.

The door flew open.

Everyone rushed inside.

Joseph slammed the emergency lock.

THUD!

One of the Hunters hit the door from the other side.

Then another.

The thick steel door shook violently.

\"It won't hold forever,\" Ava warned.

Paxman looked around the room.

It wasn't another hallway.

It was an enormous underground train station.

An old train sat quietly on the tracks.

Dust covered every window.

Joseph smiled.

\"I almost forgot this was here.\"

Sam looked at him.



\"Please tell me it still works.\"

Joseph grinned.

\"There's only one way to find out.\"

He climbed into the driver's seat and pressed the power button.

For a moment...

Nothing happened.

Then the lights flickered on.

