THUD!

THUD!

The Hunters slammed into it again.

\"The door's giving way!\" Sam shouted.

Joseph pushed another switch.

The train lights flickered brighter.

With a loud rumble, the engine came to life.

\"It still works!\" Joseph said with a grin.

\"Everyone aboard!\"

Paxman helped Ava climb inside while Sam whistled for Nash.

Nash leaped through the doorway just as another deafening crash echoed through the station.

CRACK!

The steel door split down the middle.

One of the Hunters forced its claw through the opening.

Its glowing red eyes locked onto the train.

\"There they are!\" Ava cried.

Joseph pulled the throttle.

The train lurched forward.

Slowly at first...

Then faster.

The Hunters burst through the shattered door.

They sprinted after the train, their heavy footsteps echoing through the tunnel.

One of them jumped.

Its metal claws grabbed the back railing of the last train car.

\"It's on!\" Paxman shouted.

The Hunter began pulling itself onto the train.

Sam ran toward it.

The machine swung one of its massive arms.

WHOOSH!

Sam ducked just in time.

The claw sliced through a handrail instead.

Sam grabbed the Hunter by the shoulders.

\"Let's see who's stronger!\"

The Hunter pushed back with incredible force.

For a moment, neither of them moved.

Then Sam let out a yell.

He lifted the giant machine over his head.

\"What?!\" Ava gasped.

